# UI / feed verification (mandatory)

After ANY change to feed UI, webview HTML/CSS/JS, card rendering, fetcher, cache, or auto-show behavior:

1. `npm run compile`
2. `node scripts/judge-feed.cjs` (add `--refresh` if fetcher/cache changed) — read the sample deck and reject weak/fake summaries
3. `node scripts/judge-sources.cjs` (after fetcher/cache changes) — per-source quality gate
4. `node scripts/preview-feed.cjs` — opens a Playwright screenshot of the real webview HTML with live cache cards
5. **Read the screenshot** (`.preview/feed-preview.png`) with the Read tool and confirm:
   - card chrome (title + close) is visible
   - at least one card shows a real title + readable summary (not empty, not "Quick hit…")
   - progress is not stuck on `— / —`
5. Do not tell the user it works until steps 2–5 pass

Never ship a UI change based only on TypeScript compile success.
